WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.680
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Doctor Who we got the grand tour of Coal

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:12.090
Hill School and a lot of teasers for the big
Danny Pink and Missy arcs.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:17.770
There was also a nice shout out to River Song
and Gallifreyan Clara but I’ll talk more

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.370
cool references after my Top 5.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:24.170
Quick Reminder, this week’s giveaway is
open now, all you have to do to enter is be

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.560
a subscriber and leave a comment on this video.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:32.200
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.450
But starting with Top 5 moments.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.560
Give you just a sec…

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.090
and Number 5 - The Doctor is the new Caretaker

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:46.470
Capaldi said he thought the Doctor quite liked
being a caretaker just because it put his

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.899
endless knowledge to practical good use.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:54.040
Yes his main mission was preparing a trap
for the Skovox Blitzer, but while he was doing

00:00:54.040 --> 00:01:00.460
that he was also puttering around cleaning
spills and fixing electric boxes and such.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:06.310
Plus it gave him the opportunity to show off.

00:01:06.310 --> 00:01:09.810
One of the funniest scenes was when he poked
his head in Clara’s window and corrected

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.790
Jane Austen on the blackboard.

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:17.250
I haven’t listened to it but their is an
audio drama where the first doctor and jane

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.520
austen go on an adventure in 1814.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.180
It’s called Frostfire.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:27.780
It’s just the latest in the long list of
mundane jobs The Doctor really enjoys doing,

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:32.410
like being a Curator of a museum or a Physics
Teacher.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:35.810
In the Doctor Who Extra for this episode they
stuck in a bunch of clips from episodes where

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:44.280
the Doctor worked at schools and other odd
jobs all the way back to the First Doctor.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.880
I’ll list them all off during references.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.880
Number 4 - Courtney Woods

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:47.880
This was Ellis George.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:58.049
She was in Episode 1, even though she came
back and got to go on the TARDIS I don’t

00:01:58.049 --> 00:02:01.090
know that this was a teaser for future companion.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:05.229
I think it was just a small field trip like
when David Tennant took Peter Capaldi’s

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:08.039
character from Fires of Pompeii on the TARDIS.

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:12.459
I love that the Doctor has such a predisposition
for precocious young women.

00:02:12.459 --> 00:02:16.640
Let that be a lesson to any ladies out there
wanting to be the next companion.Qualifications

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:22.140
include being really stubborn, casually dismissive
of danger and morbidly curious.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.150
She also got River’s Famous “Spoilers”
Line which reminded me of her “Mel” regeneration

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.510
from Let’s Kill Hitler.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:33.940
No I don’t think that was Mel, I just think
it was another wink at the audience.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.630
Just like the story about the Doctor living
with Otters because of the fight with River.

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:40.150
I know there have been a lot of rumors about
Jenna Coleman leaving.

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:44.360
I actively tried to not consider that when
thinking about Courtney.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:49.420
You could potentially see her scenes as the
series ‘test driving’ new companions.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.069
I don’t think that’s what’s going on,
but you can’t help but think about it.

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:57.970
Number 3 - Clara Explains The Doctor To Danny

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:01.580
This was really cool because you find out
what Clara really thinks about her adventures

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.060
deep down inside.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:12.480
The series tells a lot of parables and the
doctor and his companions get moments of reflection

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.400
all the time.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.120
But most of the time it’s done under the
guise of humor.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:19.120
Like when people get real with companions
about The Doctor they deflect a lot of tension.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.120
So you don’t linger inside their brains
for too long.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.690
It’s like Clara is trying to explain what
candy tastes like to someone who has no taste

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:24.690
buds.

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:29.300
Traveling with The Doctor is like the ultimate
fulfilment of your childhood delight.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.000
Doctor Who can be a very cerebral show in
moments like this, which is why I’m digging

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.760
Capaldi’s Doctor so much.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:38.640
He just spends equal amounts of time inside
his own head and being present in whatever

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:49.900
moment he’s in.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:53.019
Whenever Jenna Coleman really decides to leave,
whether it be this year or next year.

00:03:53.019 --> 00:03:58.099
I think we’ll get more of these big introspective
scenes, like she’s laying the groundwork

00:03:58.099 --> 00:04:01.129
for her memoirs.

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:04.470
Like her version of There and Back Again,
with the role of Bilbo Baggins being played

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.450
by Clara Oswald.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:10.860
Number 2 - Clara and The Doctor put on a Play
for Danny Pink

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:14.910
The big reveal was appropriately epic and
I love that they turned it into a school drama

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:15.910
production.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:19.500
“Boyfriend Error” definitely one of the
best one liners from the episode.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.270
They sweep the big curtain back and bam, the
TARDIS is there.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:23.749
Like they’re a couple of magicians.

00:04:23.749 --> 00:04:28.369
Which sounds even more funny after The Doctor’s
magician joke from last week’s episode.

00:04:28.369 --> 00:04:32.810
I’ve never seen Doctor Who done as a stage
play before and I wasn’t a drama club geek

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.559
when I was in school, but this felt very visceral.

00:04:35.559 --> 00:04:39.889
It also answered a lot of quesitons about
Danny Pink’s role.

00:04:39.889 --> 00:04:45.300
Samuel Anderson called himself a companion
to the companion, so yes I think now that

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.580
the curtain has been pulled back.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.960
He’ll spend more time on the TARDIS with
Clara.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.389
What’s more interesting is his relationship
with The Doctor.

00:04:52.389 --> 00:05:04.169
It seems like they’re both watching each
other.

00:05:04.169 --> 00:05:07.500
The title of the episode was The Caretaker
and it felt like we’re supposed to think

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.550
Danny Pink and the Doctor feel like they’re
Clara’s Care taker.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:13.479
In that they both feel like her care giver.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:19.949
When Danny talked about The Doctor pushing
Clara too far it felt like foreshadowing for

00:05:19.949 --> 00:05:20.949
something big.

00:05:20.949 --> 00:05:25.680
It really turned me around on the episode,
the whole thing seemed like it was told from

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:32.139
The Doctor and Clara’s perspective, so when
Danny Pink learns about the doctor, you’re

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:33.360
thinking about it from The Doctor’s perspective.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.870
But that last scene with him makes it feel
like the whole thing was being told from Danny’s

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:39.870
perspective.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:45.710
Like the Doctor, not Danny will do something
really crazy and Danny will have to fix it.

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:50.599
Just rewatch the scene where Danny calls the
Doctor on being a Lord, and the moment when

00:05:50.599 --> 00:05:51.599
he brings out the Doctor’s Rage.

00:05:51.599 --> 00:05:56.249
and my number 1 moment - Missy is Back

00:05:56.249 --> 00:05:59.069
Where are we is the big question.

00:05:59.069 --> 00:06:03.300
The person greeting the policeman said there
was a range as if he could just take his pick

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.629
of what to call it.

00:06:04.629 --> 00:06:07.949
All of the terms being references to where
you go after death.

00:06:07.949 --> 00:06:12.939
There was The Afterlife, The Promised Land,
The Nethersphere.

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:14.889
It looked more like purgatory to me.

00:06:14.889 --> 00:06:17.569
Like the policeman was in the waiting room
for the nethersphere.

00:06:17.569 --> 00:06:26.279
Missy’s character is called the gatekeeper
of the nethersphere.

00:06:26.279 --> 00:06:29.869
And when she did show up she looked very preoccupied.

00:06:29.869 --> 00:06:33.460
As opposed to her previous appearances when
she was greeting new people with smiles and

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.460
tea.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:38.220
It definitely makes her seem much more sinister
and now I’m wondering if she’s some sort

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:43.520
of cosmic entity.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:53.149
That’s what we’re being led to believe,
like she is somehow the ruler of purgatory.

00:06:53.149 --> 00:06:54.259
Some non-coporeal being.

00:06:54.259 --> 00:06:59.479
Usually it’s times like that when there’s
a big twist and the character ends up being

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:00.819
an imposter.

00:07:00.819 --> 00:07:07.479
It doesn’t seem like Missy is masquerading
as anything right now so I’m really hoping

00:07:07.479 --> 00:07:10.649
we get to see her explain herself to another
character.

00:07:10.649 --> 00:07:15.889
This policeman is one of the first characters
to question WTF is going on?

00:07:15.889 --> 00:07:20.409
So I don’t think it will be too long before
we take the next step and someone asks Missy

00:07:20.409 --> 00:07:22.159
Who Are You?

00:07:22.159 --> 00:07:26.400
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and what do you think Danny meant when he

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.849
said The Doctor might push Clara too far?

00:07:29.849 --> 00:07:32.349
While you think about that, here’s some
of the bigger references I spotted in the

00:07:32.349 --> 00:07:33.349
episode.

00:07:33.349 --> 00:07:36.669
Please add any you saw in the comments if
I don’t list them.

00:07:36.669 --> 00:07:40.729
First up is all the Doctor’s jobs, over
the course of the 50 plus year history he’s

00:07:40.729 --> 00:07:43.159
had just about every interesting job you can
imagine.

00:07:43.159 --> 00:07:48.739
The most interesting being the Tom Baker Curator
reference from the 50th, all the deputized

00:07:48.739 --> 00:07:54.400
law men he’s been and being an actual teacher,
not just a figurative one in the context of

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:55.400
the show.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:58.729
When people talk about Doctor Who’s origins
it sounds a lot like the precursor of Mister

00:07:58.729 --> 00:07:59.729
Rodgers In Space.

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:02.580
Like an educational show about History and
Science that also tells narrative stories.

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:08.469
So the Doctor has always been a teacher in
a meta context.

00:08:08.469 --> 00:08:18.419
One of my favorite tennant teacher moments
was The Doctor Loves Physics.

00:08:18.419 --> 00:08:26.619
Then There’s John Smith, the name the Doctor
used in Family of Blood

00:08:26.619 --> 00:08:32.440
The River Song reference I already mentioned,
but I felt like when The Doctor said I used

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:37.029
to have a teacher just like you, he was referring
to Gallifreyan Clara.

00:08:37.029 --> 00:08:40.370
I know everyone always wonders whether that
version of Clara became a Time Lord and I

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.500
don’t think she did.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:48.160
It seems like if she were a teacher at the
Time Lord academy she’d have a better chance

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.810
of keeping an eye on him.

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:55.920
The Giant Chessboard felt a little ominous
but Chess has showed up all over Doctor Who’s

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:56.920
history.

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:01.430
There was a giant chessboard in the Tomb of
Rassilon that was designed to be a trap.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:05.660
But you could view this as being foreshadowing
for a conflict with Missy.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:11.200
Or a visual reference of the giant chessboard
from doctor who history.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:15.329
The umbrage the Doctor takes when Danny Pink
calls him out for being a Time Lord is a nice

00:09:15.329 --> 00:09:29.440
reminder of his troubled relationship with
them.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:34.720
Those were some of the more fun nods, but
if you spotted any good Coal Hill references

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.279
from specific episodes write them in the comments.

00:09:38.279 --> 00:09:47.930
Overall I gave the episode a B plus, they
nailed the montages but I felt like the pacing

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:54.190
between the first half of the episode and
the second half was a little uneven.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:58.759
The opening Clara montage was brilliant and
I loved the music they set it to.

00:09:58.759 --> 00:10:06.509
It reminds you of the many clara’s all doing
everything.

00:10:06.509 --> 00:10:10.459
Like she has a supernatural level of energy
to match the doctor’s.

00:10:10.459 --> 00:10:17.800
And the second big montage when Clara was
trying to watch the doctor while he was puttering

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:19.470
around the school as the caretaker.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.819
That moment when Danny Pink sees the curtain
pulled back on the TARDIS is really when the

00:10:23.819 --> 00:10:24.959
action stops short.

00:10:24.959 --> 00:10:25.959
Like a record drop.

00:10:25.959 --> 00:10:29.620
In the context of the story I understand why
that was there, the change in the pace is

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:33.610
supposed to make us feel uncomfortable because
the Doctor is no longer the alpha male in

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:36.079
the room and there’s still a lot we don’t
know about Danny Pink.

00:10:36.079 --> 00:10:44.829
The stunts were all great, did anyone else
make the six million dollar man sound effects

00:10:44.829 --> 00:10:46.709
when danny flipped over the skovox.

00:10:46.709 --> 00:10:50.810
I don’t think they were making any special
references, but they way they filmed it looked

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:51.949
a little funny.

00:10:51.949 --> 00:10:57.509
I know a lot of you mentioned you heard clockwork
sound effects during Danny and Clara’s dinner

00:10:57.509 --> 00:10:59.140
date, like he might secretly be a clockwork
droid.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:06.850
I don’t think that’s the case, but I supposed
it’s possible he has some special abilities.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:19.100
He jumped about six feet in the air, so you’d
have to be pretty badass to pull 

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.680
that off.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:23.620
I was relieved to see Missy again too.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:27.279
If that’s going to be the big arc of the
season I feel like not mentioning her for

00:11:27.279 --> 00:11:36.079
weeks and weeks at a time and then just dumping
her on us would be terrible.

00:11:36.079 --> 00:11:44.939
They are making the episode less serialized
this year, so I understand why they’re not

00:11:44.939 --> 00:11:46.019
putting her in every episode.

00:11:46.019 --> 00:11:53.329
It was a great episode, but I feel like based
on what I’ve read about next week, Kill

00:11:53.329 --> 00:12:00.899
The Moon, that episode will be one of the
Fan Favorites from series 8.

00:12:00.899 --> 00:12:12.749
I’m posting my bonus video next, so check
back in about 6 hours for that.

00:12:12.749 --> 00:12:16.730
I’ve got a bunch of extra videos coming
this weekend, so I’m trying to get them

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:20.699
all out in a timely fashion without killing
myself.

00:12:20.699 --> 00:12:24.500
The Q&amp;A will post on Sunday, so you have a
ton of time to re-watch the episode and think

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:26.680
of some good Missy danny pink theories.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:29.680
Right now click here for the bonus video and
click here for the Q&amp;A.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:32.389
I’ll update the annotations as soon as I
post them.

00:12:32.389 --> 00:12:36.480
Thanks so much for watching, now let’s all
high five and go write our own doctor who

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:36.700
stage play.

